{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery contains a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). In the decision problem, Lottery A has two outcomes, each with 50% probability, so it does not contain a sure outcome. Lottery B yields -500 Euros with 100% probability, so it does contain a sure outcome. The decision reason prefers the lottery *without* a sure outcome, which is Lottery A. Therefore, the reason can be applied to this decision problem, and it would lead to a preference for Lottery A.",
